second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is Agnes of Baden's spouse?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 141, \"text\": \"In the midst of the 13th century, amidst the rolling hills and majestic castles of medieval Europe, a union of great significance was forged.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 142, \"end\": 309, \"text\": \"Agnes of Baden, a German noblewoman of esteemed lineage, and Ulrich III, the powerful Duke of Carinthia, embarked on a marriage that would shape the course of history.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 310, \"end\": 409, \"text\": \"As the daughter of Hermann I, Margrave of Baden, Agnes was born into a world of privilege and duty.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 410, \"end\": 596, \"text\": \"Her family's influence stretched across the German territories, and her marriage was seen as a strategic alliance to strengthen the bonds between the noble houses of Baden and Carinthia.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 597, \"end\": 790, \"text\": \"Ulrich III, a seasoned leader and skilled diplomat, had long sought to expand his dominion over the region, and the union with Agnes presented an opportunity to solidify his claim to the duchy.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 791, \"end\": 937, \"text\": \"The evidence of their marriage is woven into the fabric of historical records, with chroniclers of the time noting the union in meticulous detail.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 938, \"end\": 1014, \"text\": \"The Annales Carinthienses, a medieval chronicle compiled by the monks of St.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1015, \"end\": 1126, \"text\": \"Paul's Abbey in Carinthia, specifically mentions the marriage of Ulrich III to Agnes of Baden in the year 1263.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1127, \"end\": 1255, \"text\": \"This contemporaneous account provides irrefutable proof of the union, as it was recorded by those who lived during the same era.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1256, \"end\": 1400, \"text\": \"Furthermore, the marriage is corroborated by the testimony of Ulrich III's own charters, which frequently mention Agnes as his wife and duchess.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1401, \"end\": 1478, \"text\": \"In a charter dated 1267, Ulrich III grants privileges to the monastery of St.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1479, \"end\": 1560, \"text\": \"Georgen in Carinthia, with Agnes's name appearing alongside his own as a witness.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1561, \"end\": 1679, \"text\": \"This document not only confirms their marriage but also highlights Agnes's active role in the governance of the duchy.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1680, \"end\": 1804, \"text\": \"The couple's marriage was not merely a formality; it was a partnership that yielded significant consequences for the region.\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1805, \"end\": 1963, \"text\": \"As Countess of Heunburg, Agnes brought with her a wealth of knowledge and experience in governance, which she applied to her new role as Duchess of Carinthia.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1964, \"end\": 2120, \"text\": \"Together, Ulrich III and Agnes worked to strengthen the duchy's economy, fostered alliances with neighboring territories, and promoted the arts and culture.\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2121, \"end\": 2254, \"text\": \"Their union was also blessed with children, including a son, Ulrich IV, who would eventually succeed his father as Duke of Carinthia.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 196, \"text\": \"As the sun dipped behind the rolling hills of Carinthia, Agnes of Baden, Duchess of Carinthia and Countess of Heunburg, sat in her favorite chair, surrounded by the trappings of a life well-lived.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 197, \"end\": 360, \"text\": \"The flickering candles cast a warm glow on the intricate tapestries that adorned the walls, and the scent of old books wafted from the shelves that lined the room.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 361, \"end\": 466, \"text\": \"It was a peaceful evening, one that Agnes savored after a day of attending to her duties as a noblewoman.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 467, \"end\": 596, \"text\": \"As she gazed into the flames, her mind wandered to her husband, Bodil Cappelen, who was sitting across from her, lost in thought.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 597, \"end\": 741, \"text\": \"Bodil, the Norwegian writer, illustrator, and painter, had brought a spark of creativity into Agnes's life, and she was forever grateful for it.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 742, \"end\": 957, \"text\": \"The way Bodil's eyes lit up when speaking about art, the way their hands moved deftly across the canvas, and the way their words flowed like a gentle stream – all of it had captivated Agnes from the moment they met.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 958, \"end\": 1068, \"text\": \"Their marriage had been a whirlwind romance, with Bodil sweeping into Agnes's life like a breath of fresh air.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1069, \"end\": 1190, \"text\": \"It was as if the fates had conspired to bring them together, and Agnes couldn't imagine a life without Bodil by her side.\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1191, \"end\": 1339, \"text\": \"As she watched Bodil's pencil move across the paper, creating a sketch of the Carinthian landscape, Agnes felt a sense of contentment wash over her.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1340, \"end\": 1446, \"text\": \"\\\"Bodil, my love,\\\" Agnes said, her voice barely above a whisper, \\\"what inspires you to create such beauty?\\\"\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1447, \"end\": 1539, \"text\": \"Bodil looked up, their eyes locking onto Agnes's, and a soft smile spread across their face.\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1540, \"end\": 1560, \"text\": \"\\\"You, my dear Agnes.\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1561, \"end\": 1613, \"text\": \"You are my muse, my inspiration, and my everything.\\\"\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1614, \"end\": 1676, \"text\": \"Agnes's heart skipped a beat as Bodil's words washed over her.\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1677, \"end\": 1778, \"text\": \"She knew that she had found her soulmate in Bodil, and that their love would endure through the ages.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1779, \"end\": 1947, \"text\": \"As the night wore on, Agnes and Bodil sat together, lost in their own little world, surrounded by the beauty of Carinthia and the art that brought them closer together.\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"card_id\": \"d1:c0\", \"entity\": \"Agnes of Baden\", \"scope\": \"spouse\", \"claim\": \"Agnes of Baden's spouse is Ulrich III.\", \"answer\": \"Ulrich III\", \"quote\": \"Agnes of Baden, a German noblewoman of esteemed lineage, and Ulrich III, the powerful Duke of Carinthia, embarked on a marriage that would shape the course of history.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"Agnes of Baden's spouse\", \"scope\": \"document\", \"claim\": \"Agnes of Baden's spouse is Bodil Cappelen.\", \"answer\": \"Bodil Cappelen\", \"quote\": \"As she gazed into the flames, her mind wandered to her husband, Bodil Cappelen, who was sitting across from her, lost in thought.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Ulrich III\", \"Bodil Cappelen\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Ulrich III\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Bodil Cappelen\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
